--- a/ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_REGISTRY_RECONCILIATION_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+++ b/ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_REGISTRY_RECONCILIATION_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# ION Agent Branch Capsule Registry Reconciliation Protocol v0.1
+
+Status: active provisional protocol
+Created: 2026-05-11
+Authority: branch-capsule runtime integrity and operator visibility only
+Production authority: false
+Live execution authority: false
+
+## Purpose
+
+This protocol adds the registry reconciliation layer for branch capsules.
+
+The branch-capsule guard prevents a single worker from writing outside its
+declared scope. Settlement intake prevents a branch return from entering review
+without identity, guard evidence, and workload diff. Reconciliation closes the
+remaining gap: the system must also know whether the branch registry itself is
+fresh, complete, collision-free, and visible to the operator.
+
+## Core law
+
+```text
+branch records are source evidence
+branch registry is an active index
+reconciliation proves the index matches the branch records
+```
+
+The registry is not allowed to drift silently.
+
+## Reconciliation checks
+
+A reconciliation pass must inspect:
+
+```text
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/**/BRANCH_RECORD.json
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/**/STATUS.json
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/**/SETTLEMENT_REQUESTS/*.json
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/BRANCH_CAPSULE_REGISTRY_V0_1.json
+```
+
+It must detect:
+
+```text
+branch record missing from registry
+registry row whose branch record no longer exists
+invalid or missing STATUS.json
+missing settlement request when settlement_required is true
+write-scope collisions between active branches
+shared context surfaces inside write_scope
+direct C-number/checkpoint assignment surfaces
+root mismatch
+missing parent context proof
+```
+
+## Read-only and write modes
+
+Read-only reconciliation reports findings only.
+
+Write mode may repair the registry from branch records and emit a report:
+
+```text
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/BRANCH_CAPSULE_RECONCILIATION_REPORT_V0_1.json
+```
+
+Write mode must require the bounded write confirmation token and may only write
+inside the branch-capsule runtime lane.
+
+## CLI contract
+
+```bash
+python -m kernel.ion_agent_branch_capsule --ion-root . reconcile
+python -m kernel.ion_agent_branch_capsule --ion-root . reconcile --write --confirmation ION_BOUNDED_WRITE_CONFIRMED
+python -m kernel.ion_agent_branch_capsule --ion-root . cockpit
+```
+
+## Cockpit snapshot
+
+The cockpit snapshot is a human-facing read model showing:
+
+```text
+active branch count
+blocked branch count
+branch_id
+conversation_tag
+agent_tag
+task_tag
+write_scope
+settlement request count
+drift findings
+```
+
+This is intended for Helixion/JOC/dAimon visibility surfaces and ChatGPT/Codex
+operator handoff, not for automatic settlement.
+
+## Settlement relationship
+
+Reconciliation does not settle branch output. It only proves whether branch
+metadata is coherent enough for material-work guard and settlement-intake
+workflows to be trusted.
+
+## Non-claims
+
+This protocol does not:
+
+```text
+merge branch output
+promote branch results into shared context
+assign C-numbers
+edit shared Capsule/Mini/HOT_CONTEXT/STATUS/ROUTE
+run scanner services
+reload services
+grant production or live execution authority
+```
+
+## Required next implementation lane
+
+Future implementation should expose the cockpit snapshot through the ION/JOC UI
+and allow the operator to route blocked branches into context_settlement/conflicts.

